{
  "version": 1,
  "_note": "The `lockOrientation=` ROUTER BINDING (parity/F07-orientation.md \u00a73a, build log \u00a710) - the half F07 left open. The claim stack itself is already pinned by input/orientation.json; this file pins the RECONCILE that drives it: given the surfaces the router just published and the ledger of what the router has already claimed, which release/claim calls bring the shared OrientationClaimStack in line. The reconcile is a function of the LIVE SET, not a pair of appear/disappear callbacks - which is precisely why all five dismissal paths (button pop, edge-swipe back, modal drag-dismiss, deep-link stack replacement, backgrounded return) funnel into one release path and cannot leak independently, and why merely COVERING a screen (which SwiftUI and Compose both report as a disappearance) does not release it. Releases are emitted before claims so an arriving surface is never buried under a departing one, and a live surface whose `to` changed re-claims IN PLACE rather than release-then-claim. The `imperative` slot (orientation.lock()/unlock()) is never named here.",
